#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277519 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number Shown on an Argand Diagram in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90584326-4b33-57bc-80d2-a8018dd5851f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.3\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277521} {:answer/id #uuid "df9c597d-d8ac-56dd-b725-4de35d2a5554" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.8\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277522} {:answer/id #uuid "f83c4ac3-3150-5969-922e-65e28006235c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{11}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.8\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277523} {:answer/id #uuid "ac65ced2-49e1-5c54-afc6-1048b69aae55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{11}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.3\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277524} {:answer/id #uuid "0fa4696f-b63e-5d00-9f16-8cf7f8057351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.1\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90584326-4b33-57bc-80d2-a8018dd5851f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.3\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277521} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5aad4bf-4ff8-5f2d-bb23-efadfc58c28c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277520}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "98e9dda0-b7c6-5b8c-836e-5f373b899981" :question/math-academy-id "q-107428" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/assets/ba77669a8e0ffd3e69bfc8e5322d7042c318a55b4cd486ac1fac591d3b016e43.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to the nearest tenth." :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =2-3\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{3}{2})| \\\\  & ≈5.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{13}$ and $\\theta =5.3$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.3\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277526 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number Shown on an Argand Diagram in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bdea5a6-5e6f-5cdb-8c6c-e8a59b1963e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277528} {:answer/id #uuid "f46e5477-104c-5d20-ad69-057d7a1ebe6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.942\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277529} {:answer/id #uuid "ef4efc0b-98c2-5328-8f70-3b06dbc16ec2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=10\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.961\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277530} {:answer/id #uuid "4969f735-81fa-557f-a026-c1bc902ef92d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.961\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277531} {:answer/id #uuid "ea19fcd0-b18e-55eb-af0f-e9353f15c484" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=10\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.942\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4969f735-81fa-557f-a026-c1bc902ef92d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.961\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277531} :answer-field/id #uuid "992adc2a-dc98-596d-964a-c8185b3dafc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8cb4fa44-b2a4-5541-ab97-fdfc97dfb573" :question/math-academy-id "q-17516" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/assets/f13d134b7dba012b5b71a7a81ab8071b2706586699b8bf21a6df0d5c44c69619.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =3-\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{3})| \\\\  & ≈5.961.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{10}$ and $\\theta =5.961$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.961\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087999 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da227996-42dd-57ee-9cf5-5ad9542f4eb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = \\sqrt{3}e^{2.034\\textrm{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085006} {:answer/id #uuid "23ad94d0-04f3-5e2a-a228-88a865f2d15d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = \\sqrt{5}e^{π\\textrm{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085007} {:answer/id #uuid "351c9fd1-d84a-5f1e-baa1-13e88a2dc230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = \\sqrt{5}e^{0.034\\textrm{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085008} {:answer/id #uuid "5d86867e-1fba-5314-adeb-9a4b1e609293" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = \\sqrt{5}e^{2.034\\textrm{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085009} {:answer/id #uuid "7c9abc11-5fbf-5b7b-97b7-1eb3fc959f9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = \\sqrt{3}e^{π\\textrm{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d86867e-1fba-5314-adeb-9a4b1e609293" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = \\sqrt{5}e^{2.034\\textrm{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085009} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9fa440b-10b4-5ea2-a8ef-ec7da73d893f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085005}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6a6545b0-3575-5163-bc0b-11c66105aac8" :question/math-academy-id "q-17518" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=-1+2\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{-1})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-2)| \\\\  & ≈2.034.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\theta =2.034$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.034\\,\\text{i}}\\,.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277533 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5239242c-fdf3-5e96-a7e8-45892f453bac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.107\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277535} {:answer/id #uuid "717617e5-3233-5d91-88b6-89e70771a06a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277536} {:answer/id #uuid "0e112f63-cff3-51b1-9145-10c9df578f79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.817\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277537} {:answer/id #uuid "4a4a8597-e154-56ed-91d6-9041fe03a02d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277538} {:answer/id #uuid "0df0e5d1-3a63-5f80-8f27-936ecc2d1aca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.456\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5239242c-fdf3-5e96-a7e8-45892f453bac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.107\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277535} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dc6721c-942b-511f-9324-3b1411fc3665" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277534}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "087bd2ce-cf81-51d6-811a-35d764be7f1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-8075" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=1+2\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "To write $z$ in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the first quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2) \\\\  & ≈1.107.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\theta =1.107$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.107\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277540 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e10bfec-bf27-557d-8f7f-0147c7c4e6fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=6\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277542} {:answer/id #uuid "8effe772-6ad5-57d9-a5a3-04ecff3b572f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=6\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277543} {:answer/id #uuid "b67f6e9f-5154-506f-a8dd-37d2f906cd47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=4\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277544} {:answer/id #uuid "d30dcc95-fd72-51b3-92e6-cfd13275ec9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=4\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277545} {:answer/id #uuid "efa75132-ffc4-58da-8c7d-c7a5989753b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=6\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8effe772-6ad5-57d9-a5a3-04ecff3b572f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=6\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277543} :answer-field/id #uuid "50cf09ef-0e6f-52c6-b78e-007866adce47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277541}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cfd17726-5c5b-520a-a3b1-b0b99c53bf56" :question/math-academy-id "q-8078" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=3\\sqrt{3}+3\\text{i}$ in exponential form." :question/worked-solution "To write $z$ in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36}=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the first quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{3\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=6$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=6\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}.\n$$"}]}
